Description: Iron Linux Ingot desktop defaults
 GSettings defaults for the Ingot GNOME desktop (theme, fonts, dock, panel,
 tiling, wallpapers) and the login screen. Users can override every setting.

Package: iron-settings
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.6), policykit-1 | pkexec,
         iron-shell (= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: virt-viewer, ubuntu-drivers-common
Description: Iron Settings for Iron Linux Ingot
 One place for Ingot-specific settings: appearance, the Iron Tiling layouts,
 Agent Desktops (create, watch, instruct, approve, export, snapshot), hardware
 and driver management, and updates.

Package: iron-agent-desktops
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-pil, systemd-container, polkitd, dbus,
         debootstrap, e2fsprogs, util-linux, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: passt, qemu-utils, virt-viewer
Suggests: qemu-system-x86 | qemu-system-arm
Description: Iron Agent Desktops - isolated desktops for AI agents
 Runs AI agents (Claude Code, Codex CLI, AgentDock, or a plain desktop) in
 separate, isolated desktops that you can watch and instruct while you keep
 using your own desktop. Agents run in systemd-nspawn containers with private
 user namespaces or in QEMU/KVM virtual machines, with enforced CPU, memory,
 storage and runtime limits, no network or host files unless granted, approval
 gates for sensitive actions, snapshots and reviewed exports. The service is
 D-Bus activated and idle when unused; the feature is off until enabled.

Package: iron-installer-config
Architecture: all
Depends: calamares (>= 3.3), calamares-settings-ubuntu-common-data, cryptsetup, squashfs-tools,
         sudo, iron-branding (= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: calamares-settings-lubuntu, calamares-settings-ubuntu-unity, calamares-settings-ubuntustudio
Description: Iron Linux Ingot installer configuration
 Calamares sequence, branding and post-install steps for installing Ingot from
 the live medium: edition (full or lite), optional Agent Desktops, recommended
 drivers, guided or manual partitioning with optional LUKS2 encryption, UEFI
 Secure Boot capable boot loader. Live medium only; removed after installation.

